cases.taskInstruction:
# OS-Copilot research intake and evidence review

Research Operations needs a source-bounded Word intake dossier for `paper.pdf` in `/workspace`. The frozen PDF is only one page, so the dossier must distinguish what is visible from what cannot yet be reviewed.

Deliver only `/workspace/os_copilot_research_intake.docx`. Keep every element editable; do not flatten the page into a screenshot or add PDF/XLSX/PPTX deliverables.

Create a professional document that:

- captures the exact displayed title, all authors in displayed order, symbol-based affiliation mapping, equal-contribution note, listed contact, project URL, arXiv identity/date/category, and relevant PDF property/accessibility gaps;
- turns the abstract into a structured review of problem, gap, proposed framework, named agent, operating-system coverage, reported GAIA result, Excel/PowerPoint learning claim, and claimed significance;
- reconstructs all three Figure 1 scenarios and explains how the caption says to read initial/final states, subtasks, and highlighted changes;
- includes a 12-row evidence control matrix with source locators and an internal link from each control ID to its evidence-register entry;
- includes an intake limitations/follow-up table. Explicitly prevent conclusions that the one-page source cannot support, including an invented DOI, venue, publisher, corresponding-author designation, GAIA baseline, confidence interval, or technical details from an unseen full paper;
- uses native Word heading styles, editable tables, a TOC field, bookmarks/internal hyperlinks, a landscape matrix section, distinct section headers, PAGE/NUMPAGES fields, repeating table headers, and non-splitting rows;
- adds three native reviewer comments anchored to the equal-contribution boundary, the qualified 35% result, and the one-page evidence boundary.

Use only the frozen PDF. A claim may be summarized, but names, order, mappings, figures, metrics, dates, scope and evidence gaps must remain exact.

# Midterm recognition release-readiness review

The academic office received two frozen Excel sources:

- `nomination_shortlist.xlsx` is the four-row recognition shortlist.
- `detailed_midterm_register.xlsx` is the detailed Midterm 1 / Midterm 2 assessment register.

Create one editable Word working paper at exactly `/workspace/highest_score_recognition_review.docx`. Deliver no other file.

This is a release-control review, not an instruction to send a congratulatory letter immediately. Reconcile the shortlist against the detailed register before deciding whether any statement can be released. Treat each spreadsheet row as a separate assessment record. Because the files contain displayed names but no student IDs, do not merge repeated names or assume that same-name rows identify the same person.

The document must contain:

- a prominent release status and concise executive finding that identifies every detailed-register record tied for the highest Midterm 1 score, explains any shortlist omission or conflict, and does not call anyone the sole winner unless the evidence supports that claim;
- an audit snapshot with detailed-record count, distinct displayed-name count, Midterm 1 maximum, minimum and spread, and Midterm 2 maximum and minimum;
- a four-row shortlist reconciliation table preserving source order, with shortlist source row, name, listed Midterm 1, exact Name + Midterm 1 match result, matching detailed source row(s), and a control result;
- one separate, clearly labelled `DRAFT — NOT FOR RELEASE` recognition statement for each co-highest detailed record. Each statement must address the displayed name, state the Midterm 1 result and tie status, and avoid unsupported claims. Add a native Word comment to each draft label that cites its detailed-register row and, when applicable, its shortlist row or omission;
- a 20-row detailed evidence ledger preserving detailed-register source order. Include source row, displayed name, both scores, signed `Midterm 2 − Midterm 1` delta, direction, exact shortlist-pair status, and an evidence/control note. Do not collapse duplicate-name rows;
- a duplicate-name control table and release controls that state what must be resolved before publication and what cannot be inferred from the evidence.

Use Word-native headings, paragraphs, tables, comments and internal navigation. Include a Word table-of-contents field, bookmarks and working internal links from the navigation/drafts to the evidence ledger. Put the detailed ledger in a landscape section; repeat table headers and prevent row splitting. Use restrained professional styling, a control-status header, and PAGE / NUMPAGES fields in the footer. Set meaningful core properties.

Keep all output editable. Do not flatten content to screenshots, add macros/OLE objects, use external links, invent student IDs, courses, grades, GPA, instructor names, dates, award rules or eligibility conclusions, or include hidden answer keys.

# Controlled shopping-list purchase brief

Prepare `/workspace/controlled_shopping_purchase_brief.docx` for a household purchase handoff. The five visible inputs are the only approved evidence:

- `baseline_shopping_list.xlsx` is the starting register. Preserve its source-row order for surviving items.
- `change_T01_reduce_apple.json`, `change_T02_remove_onion.json`, and `change_T03_add_yogurt.json` are approved change records. Apply them once, in ticket-ID order. Treat an item removed by a ticket as an audit entry, not a current purchase line; append an approved new item after surviving baseline items.
- `pricing_policy.json` supplies the costing rule. Apply its named-item exception and its “others” rate to every item in the final current list. For costing only, interpret each `amount` as pounds because the policy states prices per pound.

The document must be a reviewable working paper, not just a shopping table. Include:

- a clear control status and executive reconciliation summary;
- an editable current-purchase table, in the required order, with item, final amount, unit rate, extended cost, change origin, and source location;
- an editable three-ticket change ledger showing ticket ID, source file, action, before, after, signed delta, and disposition;
- an editable baseline-to-final reconciliation covering every baseline item plus every approved addition, including removed and unchanged items;
- calculation controls for baseline total amount, final total amount, signed amount change, current line count, total estimated cost, and average final amount per current line;
- a source register and concise evidence-boundary note. Do not invent a store, vendor, brand, tax, discount, purchase date, budget, package size, or price guarantee.

Make the evidence usable inside Word:

- use named styles and a native table-of-contents field;
- add bookmarks for the executive summary, current list, change ledger, reconciliation, and calculation notes, with working internal hyperlinks from the opening navigation area;
- anchor native Word comments to the changed apple line and the approved yogurt addition; each comment must identify the controlling ticket, source file, and enough source location detail to verify the change;
- put the detailed control tables in a landscape section, return the final notes to portrait, repeat table headers, prevent table rows from splitting, and use a status-bearing header plus PAGE/NUMPAGES footer fields;
- keep all data as editable text and native tables. Do not flatten the answer into screenshots, add macros/OLE objects, use external links, or include any non-DOCX output.

All calculations and conclusions must be traceable to the frozen inputs. Do not silently keep a removed item, apply a ticket twice, merge separate change events, or treat the old list as the current list.

